eroid  and then once it was to a certain size  we then spiked in  uh cancer associated fibroblasts  throughout the gel itself to create this  co-culture of tumor spheroids and  fibroblasts so trying to mimic  what's happening in the tumor or the  cancer tissue itself  and as you can see the fibroblasts kind  of surround the tumor  and they they kind of like wrap around  the tumor spheroid itself  itself and they create like this this 3d  micro environment surrounding the  spheroid  let me play it again  and once again because of the optical  properties of the gel you get these  beautiful images you can do live cell  imaging  with the coal cultures as well  so this is definitely crosstalk between  the fibroblasts and the tumor steroids  which is what's happening in in vivo  application 4  is angiogenesis  so  the plates are definitely  can be used for angiogenesis assays  so what we did here was we used um gfp  labeled hubex cells  and what we did it was an experiment  where we spiked in different growth  factors to see if it could inhibit  or  induce angiogenesis  so spiking in vegf definitely increases  the tube formation or the sprouting of  the endothelial cells the vegf also  increases  and then neptrin iv is an inhibitor  of angiogenesis  and we do see an inhibition over the  control um  model  we we also quantify this it's in the  paper  that i mentioned before i just didn't  present the data here  okay so um like i said before  these plates have been used in a lot of  different applications not only the ones  i  presented here  they've been used for  numerous stem cell cultures  they've also been used for a lot of  neuroscience applications as well so  creating  these co-cultures of  astrocytes and neurons and ips derived  neurons  [Music]  it's also been used for ademy tox  applications  so we've cultured liver cells and  different  stellite cells and we've done coal  cultures of liver cells and steroid  stellate cells within the hydrogels  itself  and it works really great  if you're interested in any of this data  or other information about the product  we do have a landing page on sigma  here is the  the url on the top  and um  yeah a lot of this data is on this tech  article  it's a it's a really good reference if  you're interested in the product to  learn more about the features and  benefits and also the chemistry behind  the plates  and how to create some of these more  complex 3d cell culture models that i  presented today  i think now  that is my last slide so i think we're  on to the questions section
 

